    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0179" n="47" xml:id="pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/79a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-22T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1926—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. The protracted debate in the Senate on the World Court issue<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d40-f1"/> may delay action on the appropriation for the Disarmament
                    Commission beyond February 1. For this reason it is important that Department be
                    informed at earliest possible date whether repeated press rumors of postponement
                    of Preparatory Commission’s meeting are accurate and if they are, when definite
                    notification of postponement will be received and the new date fixed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
